laurel 2103: native canvas on the Mi A3. AppleCLCD presented the topaz iPhone X canvas 1125x2436 unless sweetfb_native=1 (not in the UEFI boot-args), so the 720x1560 panel showed only the centre 64 % of the UI (status bar, dock, home bar cut off) and the size IOMFB reported did not match the ADT canvas (disp0 canvas-width/height 720x1560). Now native is the default when the ADT says so: disp0 canvas = the panel and /chosen display-scale (2) divides both sides (360x780 points). Kill switch sweetfb_native=0 (iPhone X canvas); sweetfb_native=1 forces native as before. The layout (fLogicalW/H, fOffX/Y) is set before the rest of AppleCLCD::start, so the touch map hook of laurel 2200 (sweet_hid_set_geometry) gets the final layout. Line: 'LAUREL FB CANVAS: on: native 720x1560 at display-scale 2 (360x780 points)' or 'LAUREL FB CANVAS: off: <reason>; iPhone X canvas 1125x2436'. [U] iOS has no status bar layout for 360x780 points (topaz 0061 saw the red rdar:45025538 bar at 360x800). Self-report of this feature (was laurel 2102): 'LAUREL FB CANVAS: first frame on the panel: swap N, L layer(s), surface S WxH fmt F, canvas WxH, direct|copy path, T s after boot' at the first swap with a layer.

